row(11, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THE ANGER OF THE LORD BE KINDLED AGAINST YOU, AND HE SHUT THE HEAVENS AND THERE BE NO RAIN, AND THE GROUND NOT GIVE ITS PRODUCE, AND YOU PERISH QUICKLY FROM OFF THE GOOD LAND WHICH THE LORD GIVES YOU. {HP(11, 17, (("וחרה", "אף", "יהוה", "בכם"), "and the anger of the LORD be kindled against you — the plural 7:4, 11:17, Joshua 23:16"), (("ועצר", "את", "השמים"), "AND HE SHUT THE HEAVENS — one seat; the verb\'s Torah seats Abimelech\'s wombs shut (Genesis 20:18 — the shelf\'s proof at 306:6), Sarai\'s (16:2), the plagues stayed (Numbers 17:13, 17:15, 25:8)"), (("ולא", "יהיה", "מטר"), "and there be no rain — SOLOMON\'S PRAYER reads the clause at the Temple\'s dedication (1 Kings 8:35; 2 Chronicles 6:26, 7:13)"), (("והאדמה", "לא", "תתן", "את", "יבולה"), "and the ground not give its produce — one seat (Leviticus 26:4 \'the land shall give its produce\', 26:20 \'your land shall not give\' the fold\'s two)"), (("ואבדתם", "מהרה", "מעל", "הארץ", "הטבה"), "and you perish quickly from off the good land — 11:17 and JOSHUA 23:16 (plene \'good\'; the farewell shares ELEVEN of twenty-four, 11:16-17 read back with the heavens\' clause dropped); 4:26\'s \'you shall surely perish quickly\' the kin; \'quickly\' in this form the book\'s one seat"), (("אשר", "יהוה", "נתן", "לכם"), "which the LORD gives you — the plural one seat in the book"))} {AP(11, 17, (("ויתקוף", "רגזא", "דיי", "בכון"), "and the ANGER of the LORD will be STRONG against you (eight seats)"), (("ויחוד", "ית", "שמיא"), "and He will SHUT the heavens — the Aramaic\'s one seat"), (("ותיבדון", "בפריע"), "and you will perish quickly (eight seats)"))} The condition\'s consequence — the compile\'s hole (no cell holds the rain conditional: 9b\'s new cell with Leviticus 26 by CALL); 43:23-35 the anger\'s five retributions (43:25\'s verbal analogy on \'the heat of anger\' — Exodus 22:23, Leviticus 26:16), the exile after them all (43:29), \'quickly\' as exile after exile (43:32), the commandments kept abroad as the queen\'s jewels (43:34); the Ha\'azinu parables (306:4, 306:6, 306:9) the shut heavens against 28:12\'s open treasure.')
row(11, 18, 'MATERIAL', f'AND YOU SHALL PUT THESE MY WORDS ON YOUR HEART AND ON YOUR SOUL, AND BIND THEM FOR A SIGN ON YOUR HAND, AND THEY SHALL BE FRONTLETS BETWEEN YOUR EYES. {HP(11, 18, (("ושמתם", "את", "דברי", "אלה", "על", "לבבכם", "ועל"), "and you shall put THESE MY WORDS on your heart and on — the first-person suffix (\'My words\' — whose? the shelf reads Torah\'s); 6:6\'s \'these words … on your heart\' the kin, one seat"), (("וקשרתם", "אתם", "לאות", "על", "ידכם"), "and bind them for a sign on your hand — the plural one seat (6:8 singular; Exodus 13:9; 13:16 with the long suffix \'your hand\', the Bible\'s one)"), (("והיו", "לטוטפת", "בין", "עיניכם"), "and they shall be FRONTLETS between your eyes — THE SPELLING with the first vav (6:8 defective, Exodus 13:16 with the vav and the conjunction: the three seats, asserted on the pointed tokens); the shelf counts four from them (35:4 — the compile\'s open row since 4b, measured at its seat); \'between your eyes\' plural here and at 14:1 (the mourning\'s baldness)"))} {AP(11, 18, (("ותשוון", "ית", "פתגמי", "אלין", "על", "לבכון"), "and you shall put these My words on your heart"), (("ויהון", "לתפלין", "בין", "עיניכון"), "and they shall be TEFILLIN between your eyes — the Aramaic names the object (6:8 the same; Exodus 13:16 the same, 13:9 \'a reminder\')"))} 6:8 shares five of eight (the number changed, \'them\' added); piskaot 44 (the commandments of the body practised abroad) and 45 (the words a life-giving potion against the compulsion to evil) on the verse; 43:34\'s \'be marked by the commandments in exile\'.')
row(11, 19, 'MATERIAL', f'AND YOU SHALL TEACH THEM TO YOUR CHILDREN, TO SPEAK OF THEM WHEN YOU SIT IN YOUR HOUSE AND WHEN YOU WALK BY THE WAY AND WHEN YOU LIE DOWN AND WHEN YOU RISE. {HP(11, 19, (("ולמדתם", "אתם", "את", "בניכם"), "and you shall TEACH them to your children — the piel; 5:1\'s SAME CONSONANTS the qal \'and you shall learn them\' (the DB divides the homograph by stem); 6:7\'s \'repeat them to your children\' the other verb"), (("לדבר", "בם"), "to speak of them — the infinitive (6:7 \'and you shall speak of them\')"), (("בשבתך", "בביתך", "ובלכתך", "בדרך", "ובשכבך", "ובקומך"), "when you sit in your house and when you walk by the way and when you lie down and when you rise — 6:7\'s six tokens, the two seats in the Bible; SINGULAR inside the plural verse (2 : 5)"))} {AP(11, 19, (("ותלפון", "יתהון", "ית", "בניכון"), "and you shall TEACH them to your children (6:7\'s Aramaic \'and you shall repeat them\')"), (("למללא", "בהון"), "to speak of them"))} 6:7 shares seven of ten; 46:1 \'your sons and not your daughters\' (R. Yose ben Akiva), the child taught the holy tongue from its first words, the affirmation implying the negation (11:21\'s days shortened).')
row(11, 20, 'MATERIAL', f'AND YOU SHALL WRITE THEM ON THE DOORPOSTS OF YOUR HOUSE AND ON YOUR GATES. {HP(11, 20, (("וכתבתם", "על", "מזוזות", "ביתך", "ובשעריך"), "and you shall write them on the DOORPOSTS of your house and on your gates — 6:9\'s five tokens with ONE SPELLING CHANGED: מזוזת (\'doorposts\') with one vav there, מזוזות with two here (the lemma\'s nineteen seats; asserted on the pointed token); the shelf\'s inclusion after inclusion (36:3): ONE doorpost"))} {AP(11, 20, (("על", "מזוזין", "ותקבענון", "בספי", "ביתך"), "on MEZUZOT and FIX THEM on the DOORPOSTS of your house — TWO NOUNS AND A SUPPLIED VERB, the scroll and the post; 6:9\'s Aramaic the same to the letter but \'your gate\' for \'your gates\'"), (("ובתרעך",), "and on your gate"))} The singular verse (three 2ms) — the four tokens of 6:9 kept, one vav added; the chapter\'s shortest verse (five tokens).')
row(11, 21, 'MATERIAL', f'THAT YOUR DAYS MAY BE MULTIPLIED, AND THE DAYS OF YOUR CHILDREN, ON THE LAND WHICH THE LORD SWORE TO YOUR FATHERS TO GIVE TO THEM, AS THE DAYS OF THE HEAVENS ABOVE THE EARTH. {HP(11, 21, (("למען", "ירבו", "ימיכם", "וימי", "בניכם"), "that your days may be multiplied, and the days of your children — one seat"), (("אשר", "נשבע", "יהוה", "לאבתיכם", "לתת", "להם"), "which the LORD swore to your fathers to give TO THEM — 11:9\'s clause (eight shared); \'to them\', not \'to you\' — 47:2 reads the resurrection from it; \'swore\' no number"), (("כימי", "השמים", "על", "הארץ"), "as the days of the heavens above the earth — one seat (Psalm 89:30 \'as the days of heaven\' the kin)"))} {AP(11, 21, (("בדיל", "דיסגון", "יומיכון", "ויומי", "בניכון"), "that your days and your children\'s days may be many"), (("כיומי", "שמיא", "על", "ארעא"), "as the days of heaven upon the earth"))} 30:20 shares seven, 1:8 six; piska 47\'s nine rows — this world, the days of the Messiah and the world to come on the verse\'s three clauses, the righteous\' faces as the sun (Judges 5:31) and the stars (Daniel 12:3), the thirty or sixty ascents of Psalm 121:1\'s preposition (47:4).')
row(11, 22, 'MATERIAL', f'FOR IF YOU KEEP DILIGENTLY ALL THIS COMMANDMENT WHICH I COMMAND YOU TO DO IT — TO LOVE THE LORD YOUR GOD, TO WALK IN ALL HIS WAYS AND TO CLEAVE TO HIM. {HP(11, 22, (("כי", "אם", "שמר", "תשמרון"), "for if you KEEP DILIGENTLY — the second infinitive absolute (6:17\'s plene the kin); \'you shall keep\' with the nun four in the book"), (("את", "כל", "המצוה", "הזאת"), "all this commandment — 6:25, 11:22, 15:5, 19:9"), (("אשר", "אנכי", "מצוה", "אתכם", "לעשתה"), "which I command you TO DO IT — 11:22 and 19:9"), (("לאהבה", "את", "יהוה", "אלהיכם", "ללכת", "בכל", "דרכיו"), "to love the LORD your God, to walk in all His ways — 10:12\'s clauses (\'to walk in all His ways\' 10:12, 11:22, 1 Kings 8:58)"), (("ולדבקה", "בו"), "and to cleave to Him — 11:22, 30:20 and JOSHUA 22:5 (twelve shared: 11:13 and 11:22 stitched into the Transjordan charge); cleave seven in the book"))} {AP(11, 22, (("ארי", "אם", "מטר", "תטרון"), "for if you keep, keep"), (("למהך", "בכל", "ארחן", "דתקנן", "קדמוהי"), "to walk in all the ways THAT ARE RIGHT BEFORE HIM — the supplement (seven seats)"), (("ולאתקרבא", "לדחלתיה"), "and to DRAW NEAR TO HIS FEAR — for cleave (30:20 the same)"))} 19:9 shares ten, 11:13 ten; piskaot 48 (twelve rows on keeping the learning — silver and glass, the sponge and the well, the water and the wine and the oil, all equal in the Torah) and 49 (walking in His ways — merciful as He is merciful; cleaving to the sages, 49:2) on the verse.')
row(11, 23, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THE LORD WILL DISPOSSESS ALL THESE NATIONS FROM BEFORE YOU, AND YOU SHALL DISPOSSESS NATIONS GREATER AND MIGHTIER THAN YOU. {HP(11, 23, (("והוריש", "יהוה", "את", "כל", "הגוים", "האלה", "מלפניכם"), "and the LORD will dispossess all these nations from before you — the LORD the hiphil\'s subject, one seat (the hiphil seven in the book)"), (("וירשתם", "גוים", "גדלים", "ועצמים", "מכם"), "and you shall dispossess nations greater and mightier THAN YOU — the plural one seat; 4:38 and 9:1 the singular (chapter 7\'s find on the number, a third seat); 7:1\'s \'seven nations more numerous and mightier than you\'"))} {AP(11, 23, (("ויתרך", "יי"), "and the LORD will DRIVE OUT (eleven seats)"), (("עממין", "רברבין", "ותקיפין", "מנכון"), "nations great and strong from you"))} 31:3 and Joshua 23:13 share five; piska 50 — the LORD dispossesses and no flesh (50:1), the henchmen included and Joshua\'s labor from Israel\'s sin (50:2, Exodus 23:29-30), \'than you\' — one of the seven as great as all Israel (50:4, read at chapter 7 and reread whole).')
row(11, 24, 'MATERIAL', f'EVERY PLACE WHERE THE SOLE OF YOUR FOOT TREADS SHALL BE YOURS — FROM THE WILDERNESS AND LEBANON, FROM THE RIVER, THE RIVER EUPHRATES, TO THE WESTERN SEA SHALL BE YOUR BORDER. {HP(11, 24, (("כל", "המקום", "אשר", "תדרך", "כף", "רגלכם", "בו"), "every place where the sole of your foot treads — JOSHUA 1:3 quotes it with the article dropped and ends \'I have given it to you, AS I SPOKE TO MOSES\': the run\'s receipt of this verse (seven shared)"), (("מן", "המדבר", "והלבנון"), "from the wilderness and Lebanon — Joshua 1:4 \'from the wilderness and this Lebanon\' (seven shared)"), (("מן", "הנהר", "נהר", "פרת"), "from THE RIVER, THE RIVER EUPHRATES — the doubled form without \'great\' one seat (Genesis 15:18 and 1:7 \'the great river\' defective, Joshua 1:4 plene); the river Euphrates nine in the Bible"), (("ועד", "הים", "האחרון", "יהיה", "גבלכם"), "to THE WESTERN SEA shall be your border — the sea\'s four seats (34:2; Joel 2:20; Zechariah 14:8); \'your border\' Joshua 1:4 plene; Exodus 23:31\'s borders by other names"))} {AP(11, 24, (("די", "תדרוך", "פרסת", "רגלכון"), "where the SOLE of your foot treads (three seats)"), (("ועד", "ימא", "מערבא"), "to the WESTERN sea — the Aramaic names the side (34:2 the same)"), (("יהי", "תחומכון"), "shall be your border (one seat)"))} Genesis 15:18 shares three; piska 51 — the conquest beyond the Land only after the Land (51:1, David\'s Aram against the Jebusite), the borders that move with the conquest and the two ascents\' lines (51:2, Mishnah Sheviit 6:1), the thirty-five names of the Babylonian ascenders\' border (51:3 — the Rehov inscription\'s list).')
row(11, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'NO MAN SHALL STAND BEFORE YOU; THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL PUT THE DREAD OF YOU AND THE FEAR OF YOU ON THE FACE OF ALL THE LAND YOU TREAD, AS HE SPOKE TO YOU. {HP(11, 25, (("לא", "יתיצב", "איש", "בפניכם"), "no man shall stand before you — 7:24 singular, Joshua 1:5 \'before you\' by another preposition: the clause\'s three seats (the hitpael eight in the Bible)"), (("פחדכם", "ומוראכם", "יתן", "יהוה", "אלהיכם"), "the dread of you and the fear of you the LORD your God will put — the pair one seat (2:25 \'the dread of you and the fear of you\' by another noun)"), (("על", "פני", "כל", "הארץ", "אשר", "תדרכו", "בה"), "on the face of all the land you tread — the phrase eleven in the Bible"), (("כאשר", "דבר", "לכם"), "AS HE SPOKE TO YOU — THE RECEIPT BY \'SPOKE\': 1:11, 11:25, Joshua 23:10 the plural\'s seats, four more to the singular; SIXTEEN \'as He spoke\' in the book against EIGHT \'as He commanded\' — the register\'s seat, the finder\'s third form (4b\'s owed item); 52:4 names the referent, Exodus 23:27"))} {AP(11, 25, (("לא", "יתעתד", "אנש", "קדמיכון"), "no man will STAND before you (7:24 the other seat)"), (("דחלתכון", "ואימתכון"), "your dread and your fear"), (("כמא", "די", "מליל", "לכון"), "as He SPOKE to you (1:11 the other seat of the clause)"))} Joshua 1:5 shares five; piska 52 — \'man\' includes a nation, a clan, a woman with her spells, Og (52:1), the dread on the near and the fear on the far with Rahab\'s and the kings\' hearts (52:2), the pilgrimage\'s land guarded (52:4, Exodus 34:24).')
row(11, 26, 'MATERIAL', f'SEE, I SET BEFORE YOU TODAY A BLESSING AND A CURSE. {HP(11, 26, (("ראה",), "SEE — the singular imperative (seven in the book) over the plural \'before you\': the switch\'s two seats, 1:8 and here"), (("אנכי", "נתן", "לפניכם", "היום"), "I set before you today — the frame 4:8, 11:26, 11:32"), (("ברכה", "וקללה"), "a blessing and a curse — one seat (\'the blessing and the curse\' 30:1, 30:19, Joshua 8:34; Genesis 27:12 \'a curse and not a blessing\')"))} {AP(11, 26, (("חזי", "די", "אנא", "יהב", "קדמיכון"), "See — the singular kept — that I set before you"), (("ברכן", "ולוטין"), "BLESSINGS AND CURSES — the plural for the singular pair (30:1, 30:19 the same)"))} RE\'EH OPENS INSIDE THE CHAPTER — the portion\'s edge between 25 and 26 (chapter 7\'s form); 4:8 and 11:32 share four; piska 53 — the two ways of 30:19 and \'choose life\' (53:1), the guest\'s hand set on the choice portion (53:2).')
row(11, 27, 'CONTEXT', f'THE BLESSING, IF YOU HEARKEN TO THE COMMANDMENTS OF THE LORD YOUR GOD WHICH I COMMAND YOU TODAY. {HP(11, 27, (("את", "הברכה", "אשר", "תשמעו"), "the blessing, IF you hearken — \'if\' by the relative, one seat"), (("אל", "מצות", "יהוה", "אלהיכם"), "to the commandments of the LORD your God — six seats"))} {AP(11, 27, (("ית", "ברכן", "די", "תקבלון"), "the blessings — that you accept"))} 11:28 shares ten (the pair the same sentence); 54:1 the blessing if, the curse if not, Cain\'s \'if you do well\' (Genesis 4:7) the kin.')
row(11, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THE CURSE, IF YOU DO NOT HEARKEN TO THE COMMANDMENTS OF THE LORD YOUR GOD, AND TURN ASIDE FROM THE WAY WHICH I COMMAND YOU TODAY, TO GO AFTER OTHER GODS WHICH YOU HAVE NOT KNOWN. {HP(11, 28, (("והקללה", "אם", "לא", "תשמעו"), "and the curse, if you do not hearken — one seat"), (("וסרתם", "מן", "הדרך"), "and TURN ASIDE FROM THE WAY — THE CALF\'S FORMULA (Exodus 32:8, 9:12, 9:16 \'they have turned aside quickly from the way which I commanded them\') said of the curse; 11:28 and 31:29 the seats; five \'from the way\' in the book"), (("ללכת", "אחרי", "אלהים", "אחרים", "אשר", "לא", "ידעתם"), "to go after other gods which you (pl.) have not known — 11:28, 13:3, 13:14 (Jeremiah 7:9); \'to go after other gods\' 28:14, Judges 2:19"))} {AP(11, 28, (("ולוטיא", "אם", "לא", "תקבלון"), "and the curses — if you do not accept"), (("ותסטון", "מן", "ארחא"), "and turn aside from the way"), (("בתר", "טעות", "עממיא"), "after the idols of the nations"))} 28:14 shares nine, 13:3 seven; 54:2-4 — Moses rebukes at his days\' end as Jacob did (1:4 by CALL), the way of life to the way of death, WHOEVER ACCEPTS AN IDOL DENIES THE WHOLE TORAH (54:4 — Sotah 37a).')
row(11, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'AND IT SHALL BE, WHEN THE LORD YOUR GOD BRINGS YOU INTO THE LAND YOU ARE ENTERING TO POSSESS, YOU SHALL SET THE BLESSING ON MOUNT GERIZIM AND THE CURSE ON MOUNT EBAL. {HP(11, 29, (("והיה", "כי", "יביאך", "יהוה", "אלהיך", "אל", "הארץ"), "and it shall be, when the LORD your God brings you into the land — 6:10\'s head (eight shared); 7:1 shares ELEVEN (the same clause to \'possess\')"), (("ונתתה", "את", "הברכה", "על", "הר", "גרזים"), "you shall set the blessing on Mount GERIZIM — four seats in the Bible (27:12; Joshua 8:33; Jotham\'s Judges 9:7)"), (("ואת", "הקללה", "על", "הר", "עיבל"), "and the curse on Mount EBAL — five seats the mountain (27:4, 27:13; Joshua 8:30, 8:33) and THREE A MAN (Genesis 36:23\'s son of Shobal, the Chronicler\'s twice): the homograph for the census; JOSHUA 8:33 \'as Moses the servant of the LORD commanded\' the run\'s receipt of the ceremony"))} {AP(11, 29, (("ותתן", "ית", "מברכיא", "על", "טורא", "דגרזין"), "you shall set THE BLESSERS on Mount Gerizim — THE PERSONS FOR THE WORDS, the one seat (27:12 \'to bless\')"), (("וית", "מלטטיא", "על", "טורא", "דעיבל"), "and THE CURSERS on Mount Ebal (27:13 \'on the curses\')"))} The singular verse (four 2ms); 55:1-2 — \'and it shall be\' immediately, the entry a reward for the commandment; the blessing before the curse but not the blessings before the curses, the curses and blessings alike by the Levites in a loud voice in the holy tongue with Amen from both sides (Mishnah Sotah 7:2-5 — chapter 27\'s ceremony owed).')
row(11, 30, 'MATERIAL', f'ARE THEY NOT BEYOND THE JORDAN, BEHIND THE WAY OF THE GOING DOWN OF THE SUN, IN THE LAND OF THE CANAANITE WHO DWELLS IN THE ARABAH, OPPOSITE GILGAL, BESIDE THE TEREBINTHS OF MOREH? {HP(11, 30, (("הלא", "המה", "בעבר", "הירדן"), "are they not beyond the Jordan — nine in the book; 1:1\'s opening geography the closest kin (four shared)"), (("אחרי", "דרך", "מבוא", "השמש"), "behind the way of the going down of the sun — one seat; \'the going down of the sun\' Joshua 1:4, 23:4, Zechariah 8:7; \'entrance\' in the Torah here and Genesis 24:62 (a homograph of the root)"), (("בארץ", "הכנעני", "הישב", "בערבה"), "in the land of the Canaanite who dwells in the Arabah — one seat; \'in the Arabah\' 1:1, 1:7, 11:30"), (("מול", "הגלגל"), "opposite GILGAL — THE TORAH\'S ONE SEAT (forty in the Prophets and Writings; Joshua 4:19-5:12 the run)"), (("אצל", "אלוני", "מרה"), "beside THE TEREBINTHS OF MOREH — plural and defective, one seat; Genesis 12:6\'s \'terebinth of Moreh\' singular and plene (Abram\'s first station, at Shechem); מרה (\'Moreh\') THE HOMOGRAPH OF MARAH the bitter station (Exodus 15:23) and of \'bitter\' — the DB divides them by lemma (asserted)"))} {AP(11, 30, (("אחורי", "ארח", "מעלני", "שמשא"), "behind the way of the sun\'s entrance"), (("דיתב", "במישרא"), "who dwells in the PLAIN — for the Arabah"), (("בסטר", "מישרי", "מרה"), "beside the PLAINS of Moreh — the terebinths a plain (Genesis 12:6\'s Onkelos \'the plain of Moreh\' the same; sixteen seats of the word in the book)"))} Neither person in the verse (the third of three); piska 56 — R. Judah\'s \'beyond and onward\', the Samaritans\' Gerizim and Ebal by Shechem read from Genesis 12:6 against R. Eliezer\'s two mounds by Gilgal (56:3 — Sotah 33b), the road, the settlement and the plain as the way in (56:4).')
row(11, 31, 'MATERIAL', f'FOR YOU ARE CROSSING THE JORDAN TO GO IN TO POSSESS THE LAND WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU; YOU SHALL POSSESS IT AND DWELL IN IT. {HP(11, 31, (("כי", "אתם", "עברים", "את", "הירדן"), "for you are crossing the Jordan — Numbers 33:51, 35:10 the kin; JOSHUA 1:11 repeats the verse to the officers, THIRTEEN OF EIGHTEEN tokens"), (("לבא", "לרשת", "את", "הארץ"), "to go in to possess the land — 11:31 and Judges 18:9 (the Danites\' spies)"), (("אשר", "יהוה", "אלהיכם", "נתן", "לכם"), "which the LORD your God gives you — the plural form the book\'s one seat"), (("וירשתם", "אתה", "וישבתם", "בה"), "you shall possess it and dwell in it — one seat (Numbers 33:53 the kin); THE SAGES\' VERSE AT THE BORDER — 80:4-5 read it, wept and turned back: dwelling in the Land outweighs all the commandments"))} {AP(11, 31, (("ארי", "אתון", "עברין", "ית", "ירדנא"), "for you are crossing the Jordan"), (("ותירתון", "יתה", "ותיתבון", "בה"), "and you shall inherit it and dwell in it"))} 12:10 shares seven; 57:1-3 — the crossing the sign of the inheriting, the giving by merit, the dwelling the reward of the possessing.')
row(11, 32, 'MATERIAL', f'AND YOU SHALL KEEP TO DO ALL THE STATUTES AND THE JUDGMENTS WHICH I SET BEFORE YOU TODAY. {HP(11, 32, (("ושמרתם", "לעשות"), "and you shall keep to do — the plural 5:32, 11:32"), (("את", "כל", "החקים", "ואת", "המשפטים"), "all the statutes and the judgments — 5:1, 7:11, 11:32 with the object marker"), (("אשר", "אנכי", "נתן", "לפניכם", "היום"), "which I set before you today — 11:26\'s words: the frame closes, and 12:1 REOPENS IT (\'these are the statutes and the judgments which you shall keep to do\' — the chapter\'s last verse the next chapter\'s first)"))} {AP(11, 32, (("ותטרון", "למעבד"), "and you shall keep to do"), (("ית", "כל", "קימיא", "וית", "דיניא"), "all the statutes and the laws"))} 5:1 and 7:11 share seven; 58:1 — \'keep\' the Mishnah, \'do\' the deed, \'the statutes\' the expositions, \'the judgments\' the laws, and \'today\' as if received from Sinai this day.')

